{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": [], "hi": [], "textWords": 91, "aiWords": 0, "fakePercentage": 0.0, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/20/ebb0bc81-8ce7-4871-8bd3-116dc93ad77f", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "Fix XMP extractor returning a non-empty default entry when no metadata is found (Fixes #6577).

Problem: DublinCoreExtractor previously constructed a BibEntry with a default type (@misc) and returned it wrapped in an Optional even if no fields were extracted. This caused importing PDFs without XMP metadata to create an empty/default entry in the library.

Solution: Return Optional.empty() when no fields were populated by checking bibEntry.getFieldMap().isEmpty(). The code that enforced a default type has been removed. Also applied a tiny indentation fix in the author extraction. CHANGELOG.md updated. Changes were manually tested.", "id": 44612922}}

