{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": [], "hi": [], "textWords": 133, "aiWords": 0, "fakePercentage": 0.0, "specialIndexes": [13, 10, 0], "specialSentences": ["Testing:", "Why:", "Summary:"], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/20/c2252475-1077-4fc0-af76-53bb69fb1ba7", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "Summary:
In dark mode the icon buttons were difficult to see because the icons provided by org.kordamp.ikonli.mamaterialdesign are pre-colored and cannot be re-tinted. Instead of changing the icon set, this PR improves icon visibility by giving button backgrounds more contrast in dark theme.

What I changed:
- Added a small style to Dark.css: set .button background color to #6b727a and make the border transparent.
  File modified: src/main/java/org/jabref/gui/Dark.css
  Snippet added:
    .button {
        -fx-background-color: #6b727a;
        -fx-border-color: transparent;
    }

Why:
- The icon glyphs themselves are colored by the ikonli package and cannot be recolored reliably.
- Providing a contrasting button background makes icons easier to find and improves usability in dark mode without swapping the icon set.

Testing:
- Manually tested in JabRef running in dark mode; icon buttons are now clearly visible and the change is limited to appearance only.

Fixes: #7853", "id": 44607830}}

